{"name":"Old Botanical Garden","hex":"#5e624a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"botanical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to botany; relating to the study of plants.","Of or pertaining to plants; vegetable in the broad sense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something derived from a botanical, especially herbal, source."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/botanical"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Old Botanical Garden of Göttingen University","blocks":[{"text":"The Old Botanical Garden of Göttingen University, with an area of 4.5 hectares, is an historic botanical garden maintained by the University of Göttingen. It is located in the Altstadt at Untere Karspüle 1, adjacent to the city wall, Göttingen, Lower Saxony, Germany, and open daily."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg/330px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Botanical_Garden_of_G%C3%B6ttingen_University","wikidata":"Q570148"},{"title":"Botanical garden","blocks":[{"text":"A botanical garden or botanic garden is a garden with a documented collection of living plants for the purpose of scientific research, conservation, display, and education. Plants in larger gardens are often labelled with their botanical names and additional information. It may contain specialist plant collections such as cacti and other succulent plants, herb gardens, or plants from particular parts of the world. There may be glasshouses or shadehouses with special collections such as tropical plants, alpine plants, or other exotic plants that are not native to the local region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Orto_botanico_di_Pisa_-_general_view.JPG/330px-Orto_botanico_di_Pisa_-_general_view.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Botanical_garden","wikidata":"Q167346"},{"title":"Botany","blocks":[{"text":"Botany, also called plant science, is the branch of natural science and biology that studies the growth, reproduction and evolution of plants over the last 3.5 billion years of life on earth. As with all areas of biology and medicine, plants can be studied at range of levels from their biochemistry, molecular biology, cell biology and genetics to their ecology, pathology, anatomy, morphology and taxonomy. A botanist or plant scientist is a scientist who specialises in this field. Plants can be defined in multiple ways including approximately 410,000 species of land plants, and some 391,000 species of vascular plants, of which approximately 369,000 are flowering plants and approximately 20,000 bryophytes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Myris_fragr_Fr_080112-3294_ltn.jpg/330px-Myris_fragr_Fr_080112-3294_ltn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Botany","wikidata":"Q441"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg/500px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg/1280px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg/500px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Old Botanical Garden of Göttingen University","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_021.jpg/500px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_021.jpg/1280px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_021.jpg/500px-Alter_Botanischer_Garten_der_Universit%C3%A4t_G%C3%B6ttingen_021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Old Botanical Garden of Göttingen University","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/